    "openrouter_cost_usd": 0.075348,
    "reply": "The retrieved records describe rs334 by its variant nomenclature and a mixed set of clinical-significance labels, but none of them names an associated condition or gene. The literature variant name c.20A>T was returned [2]. The variant record lists clinical significance as not-provided, protective, likely-benign, pathogenic, other [1].\n\n## Variant Nomenclature\n\nThe literature resolution returned c.20A>T as a variant name [2]. This is a coding-level HGVS-style description, but the findings do not say which transcript or gene it is on [2].\n\n## Clinical Significance\n\nThe variant record carries several clinical-significance labels, including pathogenic and protective [1]. Because the labels disagree, the record likely aggregates different submissions, so it gives no single interpretation [1]. The findings do not say which condition the pathogenic or protective labels refer to [1].\n\n## Unrelated Matches\n\nThe search also returned rs334348 [3]. It returned rs334353 [4]. It returned rs334773 [5]. It returned c.-50T>C [6]. These look like prefix matches from the variant search rather than rs334 itself, so they should not be read as evidence about rs334 [3].\n\nIn summary, the retrieved findings identify rs334's nomenclature and show conflicting clinical-significance labels. They do not name the associated condition, so answering that part of the question needs a direct ClinVar or dbSNP record lookup.",
